<title>USA: Valero shuts 61,000 bpd fcc Houston unit.</title>
<headline>Valero shuts 61,000 bpd fcc Houston unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Valero Enery Corp shut a 61,000 barrel per day fluid catalytic cracker Monday at its Houston, Texas refinery Monday for about one week of unscheduled maintenance.</p>
<p>The unit suffered from vibrations in an expander of the FCC unit, according to Keith Booke, company spokesman.</p>
<p>The refinery, which was purchased from Basis earlier this month, has an estimated capacity of about 85,000 barrels per day.</p>
</text>
